In article <HUTTAR.94Jan6144121@hp750.itg.ti.com>, huttar@hp750.itg.ti.com (Lars Huttar) writes:
>Somebody recently posted a request for a way to permanently dispose of
>unwanted objects.  Various ways to do this within Nethack 3.1.3 were
>suggested but none of them really destroyed the objects, so no memory
>or save-file space was saved.

Not true. Putting things into bag/chest and polymorphing it does trurly
destroy them. Same for putting into BoH and making it explode.
Just checked that putting things into a pit and plugging it with a boulder
seems to destroy some of them (drop things in a pit, plug it and dig again
- much fewer objects are found). Paper objects and potions can be destroyed
by fire...

Do you believe you really can gain significant amount of memory/file space
by destroying items? Would you really want to spend hundreds of turns to
carry stuff into your rubbish bins?
